title: "Adaptive DoE: Sequential Experimental Optimization with Gaussian Processes"

authors:

* family-names: "Winiski"
  given-names: "Jake"
  orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7742-1284"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
license: "MIT"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22112432"

abstract: >
An operator-facing workflow for sequential experimental optimization using
Gaussian-process surrogate modeling and Bayesian optimization. Designed for
practical biological and bioprocess R&D, the workflow supports mixed
experimental factors, blocking, controls, randomized execution, prospective
validation, uncertainty calibration, and confirmation rounds. The project
emphasizes accessibility and reproducibility rather than methodological novelty.

keywords:

* "design of experiments"
* "adaptive design of experiments"
* "Bayesian optimization"
* "Gaussian processes"
* "bioprocess development"
* "fermentation"
* "biodesign"
* "sequential experimentation"
